https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2LuPg9U3yzo  (Capo 0)

TIP:  If transposing, play the root chord of the transposed (Gadd) adding the 5th note as necessary.

TIP:  The intro and bridge are easy to play.  To go from (A) to (Asus) and back either add your pinky to the 2nd string/3rd fret or slide your ring finger up one fret.  Reverse to go back to (A).  (D4) is (D) with the pinky added to the 1st string and when you lift it, you’re back at (D). For (A) to (A6) just add your pinky to the 1st string and lift off to go back to (A).


